Install Core Libraries:

Run: pip install flask flask-cors textblob sqlalchemy pytest.
This installs:
Flask: Web framework.
Flask-CORS: Cross-origin handling.
TextBlob: NLP for sentiment analysis.
SQLAlchemy: Database ORM.
Pytest: Testing framework.
Download TextBlob Data:

Run: python -m textblob.download_corpora.
This is required for TextBlob to work properly.
Verify Installation:

Run: python -c "import flask, flask_cors, textblob, sqlalchemy, pytest; print('All libraries installed successfully').
If no errors, you're ready.
Run the Chatbot:

Execute: python app.py.
Open http://127.0.0.0:5000/ in a browser to test.
Troubleshooting
Permission Errors: Run as administrator or use python -m pip install.
Virtual Environment: For isolation, create one with python -m venv venv and activate with venv\Scripts\activate (Windows).
Errors: Share the full error message for help.
Once installed, the chatbot is ready for development or deployment. For mental health support, consult professionals.



